ePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.1087,"playId":"401866460251","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.1185,"playId":"401866460256","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.128,"playId":"401866460260","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.1389,"playId":"401866460264","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.1403,"playId":"401866460269","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.081,"playId":"401866460267","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.088,"playId":"401866460273","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.0942,"playId":"401866460276","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.1096,"playId":"401866460280","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.109,"playId":"401866460285","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.1013,"playId":"401866460288","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.1314,"playId":"401866460293","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.112,"playId":"401866460298","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.102,"playId":"401866460302","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.0918,"playId":"401866460306","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.0925,"playId":"401866460309","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.0988,"playId":"401866460313","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.0918,"playId":"401866460316","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.1013,"playId":"401866460320","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.1031,"playId":"401866460324","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.1007,"playId":"401866460328","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.1021,"playId":"401866460334","tiePercentage":0}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"3996","guid":"a97cb83b-e9f9-3924-9940-d9dd85ceb1f7","fullName":"Yager Stadium","address":{"city":"Oxford","state":"OH","zipCode":"45056","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/college-football/day/interior/3996.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day","interior"]}]},"attendance":17156},"article":{"headline":"True freshman QB Drew Bellisari rallies Miami (Ohio) to 34-17 victory over Ohio in debut","description":"— Miami (Ohio) scored 34 unanswered points behind true freshman quarterback Drew Bellisari in his first collegiate game, and the RedHawks spotted Ohio 17 points before ending the Bobcats' six-game win streak with a 34-17 victory on Tuesday night.","story":"OXFORD, Ohio -- — Miami (Ohio) scored 34 unanswered points behind true freshman quarterback <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5280838/drew-bellisari\" target=\"_new\">Drew Bellisari</a> in his first collegiate game, and the RedHawks spotted Ohio 17 points before ending the Bobcats' six-game win streak with a 34-17 victory on Tuesday night.\n\n\r\n              Freshman kicker Brady Stidham’s 36-yard field goal tied it 17-all just 44 seconds into the fourth quarter, and his 25-yarder gave the RedHawks the lead for good with 3:55 to go.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5228762/nick-poulos\" target=\"_new\">Nick Poulos</a> fumbled on fourth down, and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5101122/malcolm-mccain\" target=\"_new\">Malcolm McCain</a> recovered. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5193270/d'shawntae-jones\" target=\"_new\">D'Shawntae Jones</a> ran 48 yards for a touchdown on the next play to seal the victory. \n\n\r\n              Poulos followed with his first interception of the season and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4893102/amariyun-knighten\" target=\"_new\">Amariyun Knighten</a> returned it 58 yards for a touchdown for the finishing touch. McCain led the RedHawks with 11 tackles. \n\n\r\n              Ohio (7-3, 5-1 Mid-American Conference) led 17-0 late in the second quarter on Poulos' 8-yard touchdown pass to <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5228764/riley-neer\" target=\"_new\">Riley Neer</a>; a 1-yard scoring plunge by <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5167252/duncan-brune\" target=\"_new\">Duncan Brune</a>, and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5156239/brack-peacock\" target=\"_new\">Brack Peacock</a>'s short field goal.\n\n\r\n              Miami (6-4, 4-2) didn't get anything going until Bellisari replaced an injured <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5388435/caleb-heavner\" target=\"_new\">Caleb Heavner</a> late in the second quarter — the third RedHawks quarterback to go down this season.\n\n\r\n              Bellisari's first pass was a 13-yard completion to <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5141795/braylon-isom\" target=\"_new\">Braylon Isom</a> and the two connected again for a 17-yard gain to set up first-and-goal. The Redhawks lost 5 yards for a false start before scoring on a trick play — wide receiver <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5293035/scoop-smith\" target=\"_new\">Scoop Smith</a> 15-yard toss to <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4876642/maleek-huggins\" target=\"_new\">Maleek Huggins</a> — to cut it to 17-7 at halftime.\n\n\r\n              Bellisari directed an eight-play, 69-yard drive with Jones running it in from a yard out for the only score of the third quarter and the RedHawks trailed 17-14.\n\n\r\n              Bellisari completed 8 of 15 passes for 99 yards and rushed three times for 64 more. Jones finished with 115 yards on 18 carries.\n\n\r\n              Poulos had 193 yards on 20-for-39 passing and rushed for 68 on 17 carries.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Ohio: Hosts Ball State on Tuesday.\n\n\r\n              Miami (Ohio): At Kent State on Tuesday.\n\n\r\n              —-\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"https://apnews.com/newsletters\">Sign up for Top 25 poll alerts</a> here. Visit <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/ap-top-25-college-football-poll\">the Top 25 here</a> and see AP’s full <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/college-football\">college football coverage here.</a>","published":"2026-11-11T05:06:44Z"}}